    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0497" n="373" xml:id="pg373"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3643</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Group to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 15.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We duly received your letter of December
                        8th,<anchor n="63" xml:id="d330-f1"/> (FE–898.51/3550), with reference to
                    the loan arranged with China by the Royal Financial Corporation of Vancouver for
                    $3,000,000. We first learned of this negotiation in September and at that time
                    made inquiry of the Park Union Bank, which was mentioned as having possible
                    connection with the transaction. Their response to us was that they knew nothing
                    about it and were in no way, directly or indirectly, interested. We enclose for
                    the Department’s information an exchange of cables with London bearing upon this
                    subject, also a copy of the prospectus recently issued by the Royal Financial
                        Corporation.<anchor n="63" xml:id="d330-f2"/> We have no information as to
                    this loan beyond the records sent you herewith.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. P. Morgan</hi> &amp; Co.<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">For the American Group</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
